# Every file here is listed in CHECKSUMS.sha256, so git must not rewrite any of
# them.  The data CSVs are written with CRLF -- that is what RFC 4180 specifies
# and what Python's csv module emits -- and normalising them to LF makes all 51
# of their checksums fail in a fresh clone.  No end-of-line conversion, ever.
* -text

# binaries: no diff attempted
*.cnf.xz  -diff
*.pdf     -diff
*.png     -diff
*.otf     -diff
*.svg     -diff
